    {
      "title": "DELETE vs TRUNCATE and RETURNING",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "DELETE vs TRUNCATE and RETURNING",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. DELETE vs TRUNCATE vs DROP",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "DELETE",
                "TRUNCATE",
                "DROP"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Removes",
                  "chosen rows (`WHERE`)",
                  "all rows, no `WHERE`",
                  "the table"
                ],
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "logs each row",
                  "fast",
                  "-"
                ],
                [
                  "Row triggers",
                  "fire",
                  "not per row",
                  "-"
                ],
                [
                  "Rollback",
                  "yes",
                  "DBMS-dependent",
                  "-"
                ],
                [
                  "Counter",
                  "kept",
                  "DBMS-dependent",
                  "gone"
                ],
                [
                  "Structure",
                  "kept",
                  "kept",
                  "removed"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. TRUNCATE rules",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:MySQL, Oracle}: DDL, ==implicit commit==, no rollback",
                "{green:PostgreSQL, SQL Server}: ==transactional==",
                "==Blocked== when a foreign key references the table",
                "Counter reset: MySQL always; PostgreSQL only with `RESTART IDENTITY`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. RETURNING",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "PostgreSQL, SQLite: ==RETURNING==; MariaDB: on INSERT and DELETE only; SQL Server: ==OUTPUT=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "INSERT INTO t (name) VALUES ('a') RETURNING id;",
                "UPDATE t SET qty = 0 WHERE id = 1 RETURNING *;",
                "DELETE FROM t WHERE id = 1 RETURNING *;"
              ],
              "note": "gives back the affected rows"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No undo",
              "text": "MySQL `TRUNCATE` commits at once, so `BEGIN` cannot save you."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why is TRUNCATE faster?** It clears all rows at once, without logging each row.",
                "**Can TRUNCATE be rolled back?** Yes in PostgreSQL and SQL Server; no in MySQL and Oracle."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Upsert with ON CONFLICT and MERGE",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Upsert with ON CONFLICT and MERGE",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. ON CONFLICT",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==EXCLUDED== holds the row you tried to insert",
                "`DO NOTHING` skips duplicates silently",
                "Conflict target needs a **UNIQUE** or **PK** index on those columns"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "INSERT INTO t (id, qty) VALUES (1, 5)",
                "ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET qty = EXCLUDED.qty;"
              ],
              "note": "PostgreSQL and SQLite"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dialects and MERGE",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Engine",
                "Upsert form"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "PostgreSQL, SQLite",
                  "`ON CONFLICT`"
                ],
                [
                  "MySQL",
                  "`VALUES (...) AS new ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE qty = new.qty`"
                ],
                [
                  "SQL Server, Oracle, PostgreSQL 15+",
                  "`MERGE`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "MERGE INTO t USING src ON (t.id = src.id)",
                "WHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET qty = src.qty",
                "WHEN NOT MATCHED THEN",
                "  INSERT (id, qty) VALUES (src.id, src.qty);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pitfalls",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "MERGE with ==duplicate source keys== errors or is non-deterministic",
                "SQL Server MERGE needs a trailing `;` and has concurrency bugs: use `HOLDLOCK`",
                "PostgreSQL: a multi-row upsert cannot touch the **same key twice**"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Dedupe first",
              "text": "Make the source ==unique per key== before any upsert."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
